est", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Accurately use information about travel and vacations in social situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn4le11ob06re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Talking About Food - Made From vs. Made Of"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the word <span class=\"italic\">ingredient</span>  to talk about what foods are used to make a dish.<br><br>For example: <br>The ingredients of cream are: milk, sugar and eggs. <br><br>You use <span class=\"italic\">made</span> and the preposition <span class=\"italic\"> of </span> to talk about ingredients that don't change their original form. <br><br><span class=\"italic\">The shu-cream is made of pastry and cream.</span>  (You can still see the pastry and the cream). <br><br>You use <span class=\"italic\">made and the preposition, from</span>  to talk about ingredients that change their form."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Wine is made from grapes. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Mochi is made from rice."}, {"type": "example", "content": "What are they made of?"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "delectable "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "delicious"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The shu-creams are delectable."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le11ob06aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use at a bakery."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "pastry"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a dough made from flour used in baked goods "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: They are made of pastry and cream."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le11ob06aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "dozen "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "twelve "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Can I please have a dozen cookies?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le11ob06aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "chewy "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "describes a food that you bite for a long time"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: This mochi is chewy!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le11ob06aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "sample "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a small amount to show taste "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You should try a sample of the mochi."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le11ob06aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to pick up "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to get something from a store "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I want to pick up some desserts."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le11ob06aud07"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Asking For and Giving Advice"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You can use the <span class=\"strong\">Wh-question</span>: <span class=\"italic\">What should I do?</span>  to ask for advice.<br/> You can use the <span class=\"strong\">modals</span> <span class=\"italic\">should </span> and <span class=\"italic\">could</span>  to give advice."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You should try these shu-creams."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You could try the sample."}, {"type": "example", "content": "What should I get? "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Who should I ask?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Where do you think I should go?"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to die for"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "very delicious "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: These desserts are to die for."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le11ob06aud08"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Choose two desserts. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make a list of the ingredients of each."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Talk about the desserts."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Tell your partner about them."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I use <span class=\"italic\">made of</span> or <span class=\"italic\">made from</span> when describing my favorite desserts."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I make a list of ingredients for my favorite desserts."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I talk about ingredients with my partner. "}]}], "type": "sena"}